Chapter: FactSyncTest
  cites Trust chapter FactSync
  cites Foreword chapter FactStore
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 Two stores that overlap but differ, reconciled. A holds h1 and h2, B holds
 h2 and h3. After a sync each holds all three, the shared h2 is not
 duplicated, and each side asked for exactly the one fact it lacked. Because
 the merge is a union over content-addressed facts, merging in either
 direction lands on the same store.

Section: Helpers

  mk : Text -> Fact
  mk (h) = Fact { hash = h, kind = DefinitionFact, content = h, author = "", timestamp = 0 }

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    let a = fact-store (fact-store fact-store-empty (mk "h1")) (mk "h2")
    in let b = fact-store (fact-store fact-store-empty (mk "h2")) (mk "h3")
    in let a2 = fact-sync-merge a b
    in let b2 = fact-sync-merge b a
    in let miss = fact-sync-missing a (fact-store-hashes b)
    in print-line-uni ("a=" & show (fact-count a2) & " b=" & show (fact-count b2) & " ah3=" & show (fact-has a2 "h3") & " bh1=" & show (fact-has b2 "h1") & " miss=" & show (list-length miss))
  end

